WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.740
A system recognises a date in your

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.085
request. Has it changed what retrieval

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.366
receives? Has it selected a different

00:00:07.386 --> 00:00:09.286
search route? Those are three different

00:00:09.306 --> 00:00:11.709
questions. Pause and decide what

00:00:11.729 --> 00:00:14.453
recognising the date alone establishes.

00:00:16.855 --> 00:00:19.240
Understanding interprets the request and

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.164
may leave retrieval input unchanged.

00:00:22.327 --> 00:00:24.600
Transformation creates changed or

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:26.636
additional retrieval inputs.

00:00:26.785 --> 00:00:29.613
Retrieval control chooses where they go,

00:00:29.646 --> 00:00:31.778
which paths run, and whether another

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:32.924
search happens.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:36.275
The chapter’s Web of Science Smart Search

00:00:36.295 --> 00:00:39.058
example asks for apple, oranges and

00:00:39.078 --> 00:00:41.095
bananas, from twenty twenty to twenty

00:00:41.115 --> 00:00:43.169
twenty four, with affiliation from the

00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:44.741
University of California.

00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:47.370
The displayed interpretation separates a

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.412
year range, an organisation and topic

00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:51.429
conditions.

00:00:51.971 --> 00:00:53.942
The structured query joins those

00:00:53.962 --> 00:00:57.035
conditions with AND, including a separate

00:00:57.055 --> 00:00:59.457
topic condition for each fruit.

00:00:59.619 --> 00:01:01.829
Inspect the visible, editable

00:01:01.849 --> 00:01:03.065
interpretation.

00:01:03.202 --> 00:01:05.347
An omitted concept or a misread

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.563
relationship changes the eligible

00:01:07.583 --> 00:01:09.921
candidate set before ranking.

00:01:10.837 --> 00:01:13.390
Primo VE NDE Natural Language Search

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.766
documents GPT four point one Mini

00:01:16.786 --> 00:01:19.730
identifying fields, generating a basic

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:22.449
Boolean query, and adding six related OR

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:24.136
connected permutations.

00:01:24.299 --> 00:01:26.907
Advanced Search receives an inspectable,

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.827
editable structured expression.

00:01:29.387 --> 00:01:31.261
That is distinct from Primo Research

00:01:31.281 --> 00:01:33.658
Assistant’s documented question to Boolean

00:01:33.678 --> 00:01:37.253
variations, CDI retrieval and embedding

00:01:37.273 --> 00:01:38.722
reranking pipeline.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.223
Do not transfer one feature’s architecture

00:01:41.243 --> 00:01:43.710
to the other. Natural language input can

00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.364
still lead to Boolean conditions and

00:01:46.384 --> 00:01:47.730
lexical retrieval.

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:50.955
Explicit retrieval feedback uses the

00:01:50.975 --> 00:01:53.236
searcher’s judgements about accepted or

00:01:53.256 --> 00:01:55.916
rejected records to help construct another

00:01:55.936 --> 00:01:57.114
retrieval input.

00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:59.370
Pseudo relevance feedback asks the

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.908
searcher for nothing: it assumes highly

00:02:01.928 --> 00:02:04.215
ranked records from an initial search are

00:02:04.235 --> 00:02:04.988
relevant.

00:02:05.537 --> 00:02:07.802
It selects useful looking terms from those

00:02:07.822 --> 00:02:10.945
results and constructs a second query.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.291
If the first ranking is off topic, the

00:02:13.311 --> 00:02:15.932
added terms can reinforce that mistake.

00:02:16.108 --> 00:02:18.755
The second pass may add candidates, but

00:02:18.775 --> 00:02:21.577
the relevance assumption was unverified.

00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:24.442
Active learning screening in systematic

00:02:24.462 --> 00:02:27.883
reviews also uses inclusion and exclusion

00:02:27.903 --> 00:02:29.906
judgements. But it repeatedly

00:02:29.926 --> 00:02:33.051
reprioritises the records already in an

00:02:33.071 --> 00:02:34.957
existing candidate pool.

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:37.071
Those judgements do not inherently

00:02:37.091 --> 00:02:39.868
construct another retrieval pass or add

00:02:39.888 --> 00:02:40.718
records.

00:02:41.269 --> 00:02:43.673
Ask whether feedback changed the search

00:02:43.693 --> 00:02:46.095
sent to a collection, or changed the order

00:02:46.115 --> 00:02:47.899
of records awaiting screening.

00:02:48.074 --> 00:02:49.858
They address different candidate

00:02:49.878 --> 00:02:50.901
boundaries.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.250
Pseudo relevance feedback needs an initial

00:02:54.270 --> 00:02:56.839
ranking before it can build a later query.

00:02:57.002 --> 00:02:58.696
It is therefore a retrieval to

00:02:58.716 --> 00:03:01.002
transformation loop, not a step that

00:03:01.022 --> 00:03:03.502
happens entirely before searching.

00:03:03.677 --> 00:03:06.234
Yet a designer can prescribe exactly those

00:03:06.254 --> 00:03:08.321
two passes every time.

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:11.209
The second query’s contents adapt to the

00:03:11.229 --> 00:03:13.606
results, while the control sequence

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:16.544
remains fixed. That dependence alone does

00:03:16.564 --> 00:03:18.876
not make the workflow agentic.

00:03:19.025 --> 00:03:22.021
Chapter Twelve asks the separate question

00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:24.237
of who chooses the next action while a

00:03:24.257 --> 00:03:25.370
search runs.

00:03:26.273 --> 00:03:29.062
An LLM rewrite produces alternative

00:03:29.082 --> 00:03:31.755
retrieval text or a structured expression.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.856
SPLADE can instead assign weights to

00:03:33.876 --> 00:03:36.704
vocabulary dimensions, including terms

00:03:36.724 --> 00:03:38.675
absent from the original input.

00:03:38.838 --> 00:03:40.467
That weighted representation is a

00:03:40.487 --> 00:03:42.979
different form of retrieval input.

00:03:43.529 --> 00:03:45.801
Both can be inspected, and either can be

00:03:45.821 --> 00:03:47.527
passed between components.

00:03:47.690 --> 00:03:50.002
Handoff between components is not what

00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:51.290
distinguishes them.

00:03:51.453 --> 00:03:53.262
Record whether you received rewritten

00:03:53.282 --> 00:03:55.930
language, a Boolean expression or active

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.572
vocabulary weights, rather than calling

00:03:58.592 --> 00:04:00.594
all three the same expansion.

00:04:01.515 --> 00:04:04.112
Keep the original request, the interpreted

00:04:04.132 --> 00:04:06.869
constraints, every transformed retrieval

00:04:06.889 --> 00:04:09.085
input, and the routes selected.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.277
If earlier results helped construct a

00:04:11.297 --> 00:04:13.712
later query, retain that intermediate

00:04:13.732 --> 00:04:16.276
ranking and the feedback decision too.

00:04:16.843 --> 00:04:19.693
Correction, mapping, expansion,

00:04:19.713 --> 00:04:22.696
decomposition, routing and coordination

00:04:22.716 --> 00:04:25.453
can coexist in one prescribed workflow.

00:04:25.615 --> 00:04:27.180
The interface label natural language

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.079
search reveals none of those choices.

00:04:30.216 --> 00:04:33.521
Inspect the generated inputs and test the

00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:35.724
candidate boundaries they create.
